# Implementation Plan - Bug Fixes for Paragraphs, Rules Export, and File Upload

This plan addresses three critical bugs reported: empty fields in the Paragraphs edit modal, failing XLSX export for rules, and "Not Found" error when uploading files in the directory.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - I will standardize the backend upload endpoint to include the `api/` prefix to match frontend expectations.
> - I will normalize linguistic data fields in the modal to support both standard terminology and paragraph dashboard entries.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Paragraphs Edit Modal Fix
#### [MODIFY] [frontend/app/linguistic/[category]/page.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Администратор/Desktop/2/frontend/app/linguistic/%5Bcategory%5D/page.tsx)
- Update the modal input values for English, Russian, and Uzbek to check both `en`/`en_text`, `ru`/`ru_text`, and `uz`/`uz_text` respectively. This ensures that rows in the "Хатбошилар жадвали" category (which use `_text` suffixes) populate correctly in the modal.

### 2. Rules XLSX Export Fix
#### [MODIFY] [backend/admin_routes.py](file:///c:/Users/Администратор/Desktop/2/backend/admin_routes.py)
- Improve the column selection logic in `export_rules_xlsx` to be more robust (using `.reindex()` or intersection of columns).
- Add better error reporting to help diagnose if `pandas` or `openpyxl` encounters a specific issue.

### 3. File Upload "Not Found" Fix
#### [MODIFY] [backend/main.py](file:///c:/Users/Администратор/Desktop/2/backend/main.py)
- Update the upload endpoints (`@app.post("/upload")` and `@app.post("/upload-docx")`) to include the `/api` prefix (i.e., `@app.post("/api/upload")` and `@app.post("/api/upload-docx")`). This aligns the backend with the frontend's API calls in `FilesDirectoryPage`.

